{
  "about": "CtrlB Relay resource keys (docs/relay-plan.md section 3, decision 6). Each case: resource and cwd (\"\" = no cwd) in, key out. Seeker's internal/pkg/relay Key and the agent package's lib/paths.py must both produce every key byte for byte. Paths are cleaned as Go's path.Clean does (note: a leading \"//\" collapses to \"/\", unlike Python's posixpath.normpath). The kinds table (docs/relay-next.md section 2) says what each key prefix is: leasable (a claim takes a hold that expires), finishable (a DONE finishes a round of work), reopenable (a REOPEN starts the next round), checked_by_hook (the pre-tool edit check looks it up) and default_lease_s (the lease of its holds in seconds; 0 is the workspace's leaseSeconds, or no lease when not leasable). A resource that starts with a prefix of the table (case-sensitive) keeps it; a path body is cleaned as a path and any other body as a name. A key of \"\" means the resource is invalid (a prefix with nothing after it).",
